What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/capacity_ranges
What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/epoch_type
What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/address_overlap
What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/postponed_overflow
What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/interrupts
Date:		October, 2026
KernelVersion:	v7.3
Contact:	linux-cxl@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RO) What the instance advertises. supported_modes,
		supported_access_types and interrupts are space separated names
		("overflow" and "level" for the two interrupt capabilities);
		supported_unit_sizes is in bytes and supported_downsampling in
		factors, both space separated; epoch_range_ms is "min max" in
		milliseconds; hotlist_size is in entries; capacity_ranges is the
		device capacity in 256 MiB units, the valid extent of the range
		bitmap; epoch_type is "global" or "per_counter"; address_overlap
		is 1 if this instance may count a range that overlaps a sibling
		instance's (a start whose range overlaps an active sibling's
		fails with -EBUSY unless both instances have it); epoch_range_ms
		shows 0 for a bound shorter than a millisecond;
		postponed_overflow is 1 if hot units survive a hotlist overflow.


What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/counter_width
What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/active
What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/overflows
Date:		October, 2026
KernelVersion:	v7.3
Contact:	linux-cxl@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RO) State. counter_width is the width in bits of the access
		counter for the current unit_size, the bound of
		hotness_threshold; active is 1 while the instance is enabled;
		overflows counts the hotlist overflows the device reported since
		the last start.


What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/damon/
Date:		October, 2026
KernelVersion:	v7.3
Contact:	linux-cxl@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Present only while the instance's consumer is "damon"
		(CONFIG_CXL_HMU_DAMON): created when "damon" is written to
		consumer, removed when another consumer is selected. The
		consumer owns a DAMON context with no monitoring targets and
		one DAMOS migrate_hot scheme; the folios of every hot unit the
		instance reports are queued on that scheme and migrated every
		100 ms under its quota. Values are unsigned decimal unless
		stated.


What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/damon/start
Date:		October, 2026
KernelVersion:	v7.3
Contact:	linux-cxl@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RW) 1 while the consumer's DAMON context runs, else 0.
		Writing a true boolean when stopped starts the DAMON context
		with the current target_node and quota_* values, then starts
		the instance with its current configuration; when started it
		does nothing. Writing a false boolean stops the instance, then
		the context, returning every folio not yet migrated to the
		LRU; when stopped it does nothing. The context is not
		exclusive: it runs alongside contexts of
		/sys/kernel/mm/damon/, but not alongside DAMON_RECLAIM,
		DAMON_LRU_SORT or DAMON_STAT, which cannot be enabled while it
		runs. Errors: -EINVAL for a value that is not a boolean, a
		configuration the instance rejects, or a target node that is
		the instance's own; -ENXIO if no committed region maps the
		instance's range or no target node can be chosen; -EBUSY if an
		exclusive DAMON context is running, or the instance's range
		overlaps an active sibling's and Address Overlap is not
		supported; -ENODEV while the instance is being removed;
		-EOPNOTSUPP, -EIO or -ETIMEDOUT if the instance cannot be
		programmed; -ENOMEM.


What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/damon/target_node
Date:		October, 2026
KernelVersion:	v7.3
Contact:	linux-cxl@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RW) The NUMA node hot folios are migrated to. -1, the default,
		chooses one at every start: the node with CPUs and memory
		nearest by NUMA distance to the node of the instance's host
		bridge (the CXL node itself has no firmware distances), never
		the instance's own node, the lowest-numbered on a tie; while
		started the file reads the node chosen. Otherwise a node with
		memory, else -EINVAL. A store while started fails with -EBUSY.


What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/damon/quota_bytes
What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/damon/quota_ms
What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/damon/quota_reset_ms
Date:		October, 2026
KernelVersion:	v7.3
Contact:	linux-cxl@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RW) The scheme's quota. quota_bytes: the most bytes of queued
		folios tried per quota window; 0 (default) is no size limit.
		quota_ms: the most milliseconds of migration work per window,
		turned into a size limit from the measured throughput; 0
		(default) is no time limit. With both set the smaller limit
		applies; with neither every queued folio is migrated.
		quota_reset_ms: the window length in milliseconds, default
		1000, at least 1. Once the window's quota is used up, hot units
		are not even queued until the next window; queued folios the
		quota does not cover are returned to the LRU, not kept. A store
		while started fails with -EBUSY; a value that is not an
		unsigned number, or below the minimum, with -EINVAL.


What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/damon/sz_tried
What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/damon/sz_applied
What:		/sys/bus/cxl/devices/hmu_memX.Y/hmu_memX.Y.Z/damon/qt_exceeds
Date:		October, 2026
KernelVersion:	v7.3
Contact:	linux-cxl@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RO) The scheme's statistics for the current run, or the last
		one once stopped; 0 until the first start after "damon" is
		selected, and reset by every start. sz_tried: bytes of queued
		folios considered within the quota; sz_applied: bytes
		migrated; qt_exceeds: quota windows that ended with the quota
		used up.
